[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

3
00:00:09.253 --> 00:00:10.253
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

4
00:00:10.253 --> 00:00:11.253
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

5
00:00:16.561 --> 00:00:17.585
[The Salvation Army Red Kettle]

6
00:00:23.725 --> 00:00:25.933
Merry Christmas!

7
00:00:32.493 --> 00:00:35.181
Merry Christmas!

8
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:43.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

9
00:00:48.589 --> 00:00:50.869
What is it?

10
00:01:22.486 --> 00:01:24.153
Ji Ah. I got you a present.

11
00:01:24.153 --> 00:01:27.186
Wow! A teddy bear!

12
00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:29.820
Thank you so much. Daddy!

13
00:02:06.186 --> 00:02:10.253
It's been seven years
since I last saw your face.

14
00:02:10.253 --> 00:02:15.420
I've missed you so much all that time.

15
00:02:21.261 --> 00:02:27.520
More than anything.
I'm sorry for leaving you all alone.

16
00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:33.220
I've blamed myself every single day.

17
00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.686
That day...

18
00:02:38.686 --> 00:02:41.386
I shouldn't have done that that day.

19
00:02:50.986 --> 00:02:55.320
I think something got into it.
I'll get you another one.

20
00:03:08.286 --> 00:03:10.453
You turned out so well. my daughter.

21
00:03:10.453 --> 00:03:15.720
Now that I see you.
you look just like your late mom.

22
00:03:18.186 --> 00:03:20.853
For seven years in prison.

23
00:03:20.853 --> 00:03:24.720
I stared at the ceiling every night.
filled with regret.

24
00:03:25.953 --> 00:03:27.720
That day...

25
00:03:32.986 --> 00:03:36.320
I should've killed you too.

26
00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:39.086
- Let go!
- You ungrateful brat!

27
00:03:39.086 --> 00:03:41.220
After everything I did for you.
you reported your own dad?

28
00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:45.420
Do you have any idea how long
I've been waiting for this day?

29
00:03:48.186 --> 00:03:50.053
You little...

30
00:03:52.557 --> 00:03:54.097
You brat.

31
00:03:55.286 --> 00:03:57.253
Where do you think you're going?

32
00:03:58.986 --> 00:04:02.253
I'll finish what I should've done back then.

33
00:04:04.301 --> 00:04:06.061
You little brat.

34
00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:11.053
Get over here. Get over here!

35
00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:22.353
Stay still. you punk.

36
00:04:22.353 --> 00:04:23.986
The more you struggle.
the harder it'll be on you.

37
00:04:23.986 --> 00:04:25.877
Relax...

38
00:04:26.853 --> 00:04:30.753
It's time for you to go meet your mom too.

39
00:05:19.129 --> 00:05:21.221
[Machine Wash]

40
00:05:55.402 --> 00:05:56.341
[Merry Christmas]

41
00:05:56.365 --> 00:05:59.286
Do you want a Christmas present?

42
00:06:00.486 --> 00:06:02.720
Then no crying.

43
00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:06.686
You have to be good.

44
00:06:07.353 --> 00:06:11.245
I heard that Santa is very clear
about right and wrong.

45
00:06:11.245 --> 00:06:12.886
Miss. who are you?

46
00:06:12.886 --> 00:06:17.453
Leave the living room window
slightly open when you get home.

47
00:06:17.453 --> 00:06:19.553
And leave the lights on.

48
00:06:26.286 --> 00:06:27.953
See you again.

49
00:07:17.277 --> 00:07:22.900
[15 Years Later. Present Day]

50
00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.920
Mommy. wake up!

51
00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:42.753
Yul. you're awake?

52
00:07:42.753 --> 00:07:44.353
Daddy. wake up too!

53
00:07:44.353 --> 00:07:46.186
Five more minutes. just five...

54
00:07:46.186 --> 00:07:50.186
No. you have to go to work!

55
00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:54.553
Yul really takes after you.
no doubt about it.

56
00:07:54.553 --> 00:07:57.486
Jeez. she's listening.

57
00:07:57.486 --> 00:08:01.986
My Yul. you're so smart
because you take after your daddy.

58
00:08:01.986 --> 00:08:03.886
Are you awake?

59
00:08:03.886 --> 00:08:05.686
Really?

60
00:08:05.686 --> 00:08:07.820
Are you so smart
because you take after me. Yul?

61
00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:08.920
Yul. come here!

62
00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:11.420
Daddy. get up already.

63
00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:15.353
Oh. my little precious. Come here.

64
00:08:15.353 --> 00:08:17.253
Yul. did you sleep well?

65
00:08:17.986 --> 00:08:20.013
I think we put her to bed too early.

66
00:08:20.013 --> 00:08:24.153
Well. who was it that insisted
on putting her to bed so early?

67
00:08:24.153 --> 00:08:26.020
Was that me?

68
00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:29.886
Then our big precious too...

69
00:08:29.886 --> 00:08:32.020
I need to go potty.

70
00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:34.286
- Potty...
- Let's go potty.

71
00:08:34.286 --> 00:08:37.486
Come on. Let's go potty.

72
00:08:37.486 --> 00:08:40.453
Let's go! Let's go potty.

73
00:08:45.097 --> 00:08:47.407
[Episode 1]

74
00:09:02.186 --> 00:09:05.786
The monster's coming after you!
I'll catch you!

75
00:09:05.786 --> 00:09:11.213
Let's go! Yul. let's go! Come on!

76
00:09:17.921 --> 00:09:20.013
[Kwon Yul. Dad. Mom]

77
00:09:44.186 --> 00:09:45.620
All done! Let's go!

78
00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:47.353
Daddy! The swings!

79
00:09:47.353 --> 00:09:49.786
The swings!

80
00:09:54.125 --> 00:09:55.725
Well. it's good. right?

81
00:09:56.386 --> 00:09:58.986
Four-year-olds can eat on their own. right?

82
00:09:58.986 --> 00:10:00.053
Yeah.

83
00:10:00.053 --> 00:10:03.486
Go ahead. Yul. Try eating by yourself.

84
00:10:03.486 --> 00:10:06.253
Time for an important decision.

85
00:10:06.253 --> 00:10:10.686
The selfish new look. bought with money
stashed away from my wife.

86
00:10:10.686 --> 00:10:14.420
Or the rebellious night out. lying about
working late and heading to the club.

87
00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:16.053
Which one?

88
00:10:17.186 --> 00:10:19.469
The rebel look today?

89
00:10:19.469 --> 00:10:22.220
Oh. my! Really?

90
00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:25.420
Wow. my wife is so generous.

91
00:10:27.453 --> 00:10:29.986
When was the last time I went clubbing?

92
00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:33.220
Yul. did you eat it all by yourself?

93
00:10:33.220 --> 00:10:35.586
Awesome! You can eat all by yourself now!

94
00:10:35.586 --> 00:10:39.120
Daddy! Yul finished all her food.

95
00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:41.986
Really? You ate it all by yourself?

96
00:10:43.286 --> 00:10:45.220
That's amazing. my girl!

97
00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:47.153
What time is it? Oh. time to get dressed.

98
00:10:47.153 --> 00:10:48.353
Let's go!

99
00:10:48.353 --> 00:10:51.253
Let's go. let's go! Let's get you changed.

100
00:10:51.253 --> 00:10:53.953
Honey. her P.E. uniform is over there.

101
00:10:53.953 --> 00:10:55.253
Yul. do you have P.E. today?

102
00:10:55.253 --> 00:10:56.486
- Yeah.
- That's nice.

103
00:10:56.486 --> 00:10:57.786
- What time is it?
- Okay. then.

104
00:10:57.786 --> 00:11:00.086
stand on one foot for five seconds.

105
00:11:00.086 --> 00:11:01.353
Start!

106
00:11:01.353 --> 00:11:02.953
One. two. three. four. five!

107
00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:05.453
Success!

108
00:11:05.453 --> 00:11:08.120
- Success!
- Success!

109
00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:11.053
- One. two. three!
- One. two. three!

110
00:11:11.053 --> 00:11:13.920
- One. two. three!
- One more time. One. two. three!

111
00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:16.486
Have fun with your friends. See you tonight!

112
00:11:16.486 --> 00:11:18.797
- Okay! Bye-bye!
- Bye-bye!

113
00:11:18.797 --> 00:11:20.120
Here.

114
00:11:22.486 --> 00:11:23.686
What?

115
00:11:23.686 --> 00:11:28.173
I feel like I had an important reason
to get off work early today.

116
00:11:28.173 --> 00:11:30.086
What was it?

117
00:11:33.586 --> 00:11:35.986
Seriously. what was it?

118
00:11:35.986 --> 00:11:38.186
Well. what could it be?

119
00:11:39.986 --> 00:11:41.686
You're not falling for it. huh?

120
00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:48.086
I'll be home early today.
For my honey's big day tomorrow.

121
00:11:48.086 --> 00:11:50.320
Oh. stop it.

122
00:11:51.386 --> 00:11:55.120
But if you'd forgotten.
you would've been in big trouble.

123
00:11:55.953 --> 00:11:57.820
I really hope not.

124
00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:59.620
Right.

125
00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:05.653
Ms. Yoo Bo Na. have a great day today.
And I'll see you this evening.

126
00:12:05.653 --> 00:12:07.286
Alright.

127
00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:09.453
What about what we didn't do earlier?

128
00:12:09.453 --> 00:12:11.053
Now!

129
00:12:11.053 --> 00:12:12.553
I'll get going. Bye-bye.

130
00:12:12.553 --> 00:12:14.053
- Bye!
- Me too!

131
00:12:14.053 --> 00:12:15.086
A kiss for Yul too!

132
00:12:15.086 --> 00:12:17.320
A kiss for Yul too! Bye!

133
00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:18.320
Bye-bye!

134
00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:19.486
- See you later.
- Have a good day!

135
00:12:19.486 --> 00:12:22.086
- I'll get going.
- Yul. I'm closing the door.

136
00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:27.786
<i>♪ Baby shark. doo. doo. doo. doo ♪</i>

137
00:12:27.786 --> 00:12:30.637
<i>♪ Yul shark. doo. doo. doo. doo ♪</i>

138
00:12:30.637 --> 00:12:33.153
<i>♪ Mommy shark. doo. doo. doo. doo ♪</i>

139
00:12:33.153 --> 00:12:35.520
<i>♪ Daddy shark. doo. doo. doo. doo ♪</i>

140
00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:37.120
<i>♪ Grandma ♪</i>

141
00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:41.786
<i>♪ Doo. doo. doo. doo ♪</i>

142
00:12:55.253 --> 00:12:57.320
Yul. shall we sing the song again?

143
00:12:57.320 --> 00:13:01.520
<i>♪ Daddy shark. doo. doo. doo. doo ♪</i>

144
00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:05.386
Yes. yes. Don't run! Be careful. careful!

145
00:13:06.153 --> 00:13:07.753
- Goodbye!
- Yeah. yeah.

146
00:13:07.753 --> 00:13:08.886
Take care.

147
00:13:08.886 --> 00:13:11.053
Seo Jun!

148
00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:12.720
Up you go.

149
00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:14.020
Please take good care of him today.

150
00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:15.553
Be sure to listen to your teacher. okay?

151
00:13:15.553 --> 00:13:17.620
- I'll be off.
- Okay. have a good day. Ma'am.

152
00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:19.420
- Hello!
- Hello!

153
00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:21.653
Hello.

154
00:13:21.653 --> 00:13:23.886
Hello!

155
00:13:23.886 --> 00:13:25.986
- Hello.
- Hello!

156
00:13:25.986 --> 00:13:29.653
She always looks so relaxed. It's nice.

157
00:13:29.653 --> 00:13:30.686
- Yul. you're here!
- Hello.

158
00:13:30.686 --> 00:13:33.186
Miss. I ate breakfast all by myself today.

159
00:13:33.186 --> 00:13:36.720
Oh. really? You did a great job.

160
00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:38.386
Yul. say hello to your teacher first.

161
00:13:38.386 --> 00:13:41.820
- Give her a nice big bow.
- Good morning.

162
00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:43.453
Please take good care of her today too.

163
00:13:43.453 --> 00:13:46.386
Don't worry. Yul seems to have adjusted now.

164
00:13:46.386 --> 00:13:49.486
Totally different from the beginning.
she's playing well and doing great.

165
00:13:49.486 --> 00:13:51.886
That's thanks to you. Thank you.

166
00:13:51.886 --> 00:13:53.886
Yul. shall we say goodbye to Mommy today?

167
00:13:53.886 --> 00:13:55.753
Okay. My Yul.

168
00:13:55.753 --> 00:13:57.586
- Today. too. with friends.
- Today. too. with friends.

169
00:13:57.586 --> 00:13:59.486
- get along well!
- get along well!

170
00:13:59.486 --> 00:14:01.086
- Have a nice day!
- Yul. let's go.

171
00:14:01.086 --> 00:14:02.320
Have a good day. Ma'am. See you later.

172
00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:05.586
- Okay.
- Yul's mom!

173
00:14:05.586 --> 00:14:08.353
How about a morning coffee for a change?

174
00:14:08.353 --> 00:14:09.986
That sounds great.

175
00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:15.653
Oh. Ye Geon's mom.
did you not sleep well last night?

176
00:14:15.653 --> 00:14:18.253
My kid dozed off poorly
in the early evening. woke up.

177
00:14:18.253 --> 00:14:20.686
and then couldn't fall back asleep
until late at night.

178
00:14:20.686 --> 00:14:22.553
- Oh. dear. really?
- See?

179
00:14:22.553 --> 00:14:24.253
I told you. right?

180
00:14:24.253 --> 00:14:27.286
That's why you need to
stick to a daily routine.

181
00:14:27.286 --> 00:14:29.986
Otherwise. you'll end up twice as exhausted.

182
00:14:29.986 --> 00:14:36.437
Look at me. No matter how tired I am.
I never let my kid nap during the day.

183
00:14:37.053 --> 00:14:39.120
Right. naps...

184
00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:42.420
By the way. isn't Seo Jun's mom amazing?

185
00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:46.453
I saw earlier that she even seemed
to forget that today was P.E. day.

186
00:14:46.453 --> 00:14:50.653
I don't know how she manages
to work while raising a child.

187
00:14:52.653 --> 00:14:55.820
I'll... I'll go get it. You stay here.

188
00:14:57.853 --> 00:15:01.353
How can you say that
after seeing that poor child earlier?

189
00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:08.786
If you can't do both properly.
you should just focus on one thing.

190
00:15:08.786 --> 00:15:09.920
Oh. dear.

191
00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:12.853
I just feel sorry for her.

192
00:15:13.733 --> 00:15:14.733
Oh. well.

193
00:15:14.733 --> 00:15:15.820
Thank you!

194
00:15:15.820 --> 00:15:17.720
The latte...

195
00:15:18.853 --> 00:15:21.653
Still. I envy Seo Jun's mom sometimes.

196
00:15:21.653 --> 00:15:25.020
It's hard. but at least
she gets to keep working.

197
00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:28.986
I only planned to take a short break.
but sometimes I regret staying home.

198
00:15:28.986 --> 00:15:30.020
Me too.

199
00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:34.586
After spending all day dealing with my kid.
I sometimes miss working outside too.

200
00:15:34.586 --> 00:15:36.753
Who wouldn't want to keep working?

201
00:15:36.753 --> 00:15:40.020
Is there anyone here
who doesn't want to work?

202
00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:42.453
That's why I call it being greedy.

203
00:15:42.453 --> 00:15:45.086
Kids need so much attention at that age.

204
00:15:45.086 --> 00:15:48.686
How can you leave them and work?

205
00:15:48.686 --> 00:15:50.853
Is it really impossible?

206
00:15:52.253 --> 00:15:54.853
Is it really that hard to work
while raising a child?

207
00:15:54.853 --> 00:15:57.386
I really hope not...

208
00:15:57.386 --> 00:15:59.353
Why?

209
00:15:59.353 --> 00:16:01.986
I'm going back to work starting tomorrow.

210
00:16:01.986 --> 00:16:02.986
Oh. my.

211
00:16:02.986 --> 00:16:09.320
My parental leave ends today.
so I'm going back to work tomorrow...

212
00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:12.553
Wait. you were a working mom this whole time?

213
00:16:12.553 --> 00:16:15.520
How did we not know?

214
00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:19.553
What. so you were just
taking a break from work?

215
00:16:19.553 --> 00:16:21.120
How long were you off work?

216
00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:23.953
- One year?
- Three years.

217
00:16:24.686 --> 00:16:26.886
I wanted to wait until my child
was a little older before going back...

218
00:16:26.886 --> 00:16:28.686
Three years? Are you a civil servant?

219
00:16:28.686 --> 00:16:30.553
Or do you work for a major company?

220
00:16:30.553 --> 00:16:33.753
No. I just work for a small company.

221
00:16:34.420 --> 00:16:36.420
A small company.

222
00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:38.220
Small...

223
00:16:40.086 --> 00:16:45.586
I really enjoyed having
morning coffee together like this.

224
00:16:45.586 --> 00:16:48.786
and learning parenting tips from you all.

225
00:16:48.786 --> 00:16:51.486
And the coffee here is so delicious. right?

226
00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:09.553
<i>Today is D-Day. Soryong Nightclub. Musan.</i>

227
00:17:09.553 --> 00:17:14.220
Today? Why does it have to be today?

228
00:17:15.186 --> 00:17:19.420
This won't do. This is a problem.

229
00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:21.753
I'm really in trouble now. Oh. my.

230
00:17:23.386 --> 00:17:26.886
Honey. I'm sorry. Really.
But this D-day was scheduled first...

231
00:17:26.886 --> 00:17:29.786
I'll really make it up to you.

232
00:17:36.808 --> 00:17:37.705
[Mother]

233
00:17:38.453 --> 00:17:40.973
Mother? Yes.

234
00:17:40.973 --> 00:17:43.757
Yeah. it's fine. Go ahead.

235
00:17:45.986 --> 00:17:47.720
It must be a great company.

236
00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:50.286
It's not easy to take the full three years
of parental leave.

237
00:17:50.286 --> 00:17:53.486
Or maybe she's just really capable?

238
00:17:53.486 --> 00:17:57.420
Well. she's been off for three years.
Why bother going back now...

239
00:17:59.553 --> 00:18:00.886
I got it!

240
00:18:00.886 --> 00:18:01.953
What is it?

241
00:18:01.953 --> 00:18:03.953
The husband must be
struggling financially. I guess.

242
00:18:03.953 --> 00:18:07.153
- Oh. no.
- That must have been hard.

243
00:18:07.153 --> 00:18:08.486
She never told us.

244
00:18:08.486 --> 00:18:11.820
Well. she has to earn her own money. I guess.

245
00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:17.120
<i>More than half of the drug cases
uncovered by police in recent months</i>

246
00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:20.753
<i>have involved people in their 20s and 30s.</i>

247
00:18:20.753 --> 00:18:24.720
<i>New types of drugs. including
liquid marijuana. ketamine. and fentanyl.</i>

248
00:18:24.720 --> 00:18:26.586
<i>are reportedly spreading</i>

249
00:18:26.586 --> 00:18:31.953
<i>among ordinary office workers and students
through clubs and private academies.</i>

250
00:18:37.686 --> 00:18:40.020
Mother. I'm here! Hello. Sister-in-law.

251
00:18:40.020 --> 00:18:42.820
Oh. my. you're here. What brings you here?

252
00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:45.086
I made some radish kimchi
that Tae Seong likes.

253
00:18:45.086 --> 00:18:47.353
Oh. radish kimchi?

254
00:18:48.720 --> 00:18:51.853
Let me get that. Mother. Just leave it.

255
00:18:51.853 --> 00:18:55.453
Wow. it looks so appetizing
just from the sight of it.

256
00:18:55.453 --> 00:18:59.553
My mom sure has all kinds of excuses
to call her daughter-in-law over.

257
00:18:59.553 --> 00:19:02.053
Will my son even eat properly
starting tomorrow?

258
00:19:02.053 --> 00:19:04.920
Don't worry. Mother.
I'll make sure he eats well.

259
00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:07.186
No wonder you treat him
like your precious only son.

260
00:19:07.186 --> 00:19:09.386
I'm sure she'll take good care of him.

261
00:19:09.386 --> 00:19:13.320
These days. daughters-in-law don't really
like their mothers-in-law fussing over them.

262
00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:14.520
Is that so?

263
00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:16.953
No. Mother. I really appreciate it.

264
00:19:16.953 --> 00:19:19.853
Thank you. Mother. We'll enjoy it.

265
00:19:19.853 --> 00:19:25.486
No matter how busy I was.
I've never fed my family instant food.

266
00:19:25.486 --> 00:19:27.286
I'll keep that in mind. Mother.

267
00:19:27.286 --> 00:19:33.381
Speaking of which. Mother.
that soy-marinated crab. jellyfish salad.

268
00:19:33.381 --> 00:19:34.381
and pickled perilla leaves
you made last time.

269
00:19:34.381 --> 00:19:36.620
could you make them again?

270
00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:39.553
- Huh?
- Tae Seong really loved them.

271
00:19:39.553 --> 00:19:41.186
We finished them in less than three days.

272
00:19:41.186 --> 00:19:43.420
Oh. sure. I'll make them.

273
00:19:43.420 --> 00:19:45.620
Really? Thank you.

274
00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:47.420
Is there anything
I can help you with. Mother?

275
00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:51.420
Oh. no. just go quickly.
You probably have a lot to prepare.

276
00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:52.586
- No. it's fine.
- Oh. my.

277
00:19:52.586 --> 00:19:56.053
Why does my shoulder hurt so much today?

278
00:19:56.053 --> 00:19:57.520
- When am I going to finish all this...
- Mother. leave it.

279
00:19:57.520 --> 00:20:00.020
- I'll do it. Leave it.
- Mother!

280
00:20:05.953 --> 00:20:08.220
Okay. let's do this.

281
00:20:17.286 --> 00:20:20.120
Oh. Mom. really...

282
00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:23.620
Do you really have to work her
on her last day off?

283
00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:26.486
I'm not making her do anything.
She offered to do it.

284
00:20:26.486 --> 00:20:27.886
Oh. dear.

285
00:20:27.886 --> 00:20:30.153
- What?
- Oh. hello.

286
00:20:30.153 --> 00:20:32.020
Is your daughter-in-law
going back to work tomorrow?

287
00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:33.953
She's returning to work or something.

288
00:20:33.953 --> 00:20:36.520
Oh! That's good.

289
00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:40.086
It's hard to make a living on
one income these days.

290
00:20:40.086 --> 00:20:43.120
My son has been working himself
to the bone supporting the family alone.

291
00:20:43.120 --> 00:20:44.786
So. was she just sitting around
all this time?

292
00:20:44.786 --> 00:20:48.686
Jeez. I'm sure her salary
is barely anything anyway.

293
00:20:48.686 --> 00:20:50.120
She's already acting all high and mighty.

294
00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:51.753
Mom!

295
00:20:51.753 --> 00:20:53.853
When did she ever act like that?

296
00:20:53.853 --> 00:20:58.020
Didn't you say your daughter-in-law
worked for some big company?

297
00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:00.053
Was it some place
that sells refrigerators and TVs?

298
00:21:00.053 --> 00:21:02.220
You're talking nonsense.

299
00:21:02.220 --> 00:21:05.553
That one. She works for that fan company.

300
00:21:08.286 --> 00:21:09.653
I need to replace my fan.

301
00:21:09.653 --> 00:21:12.220
Can you get an employee discount
or something?

302
00:21:12.220 --> 00:21:14.453
They probably don't make much money
selling those anyway.

303
00:21:14.453 --> 00:21:16.653
Anyway. why are you here?

304
00:21:16.653 --> 00:21:17.886
- Did you hear?
- Hear what?

305
00:21:17.886 --> 00:21:22.320
That Chinese restaurant in the front
shopping area is closing down.

306
00:21:22.320 --> 00:21:25.786
What? Isn't that the place
where people line up to eat?

307
00:21:25.786 --> 00:21:27.053
Why are they suddenly closing?

308
00:21:27.053 --> 00:21:30.553
Apparently the building owner
tripled the rent.

309
00:21:30.553 --> 00:21:32.486
- Oh. my.
- What else could it mean?

310
00:21:32.486 --> 00:21:33.486
They're telling them to leave.

311
00:21:33.486 --> 00:21:35.620
Wow. that's really nasty.

312
00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:39.053
Since business is good. they want to
open their own restaurant there.

313
00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:46.469
[Tae Seong Chicken]

314
00:21:55.832 --> 00:21:57.077
[Big sale today:
30% off select industrial products]

315
00:21:57.101 --> 00:21:59.086
[50% off all agricultural products]
Oh. the mart is having a sale.

316
00:22:18.886 --> 00:22:21.520
At least I've been lucky with my landlord.

317
00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:23.986
The rent for all the shops around here
goes up every year.

318
00:22:23.986 --> 00:22:26.386
but mine has stayed the same for five years.

319
00:22:26.386 --> 00:22:28.120
It'll probably stay that way
this time too. right?

320
00:22:28.120 --> 00:22:29.120
I guess so.

321
00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:32.886
Oh! Oh. my gosh! You're being too naive.

322
00:22:32.886 --> 00:22:35.086
How can you be so sure
about someone's intentions?

323
00:22:35.086 --> 00:22:39.053
After five years frozen. they could raise it
all at once. and we'd have no say.

324
00:22:39.053 --> 00:22:41.353
Oh. no way!

325
00:22:41.353 --> 00:22:44.453
Business isn't even good these days.

326
00:22:55.620 --> 00:22:57.186
If you're really worried.

327
00:22:57.186 --> 00:23:00.720
you should visit the landlord beforehand
and show some appreciation.

328
00:23:00.720 --> 00:23:03.553
Who could say no to a smiling face?

329
00:23:08.220 --> 00:23:11.386
Sun Il. let's go buy a gift right now.

330
00:23:11.386 --> 00:23:14.753
The landlord must be loaded.
What are you going to buy?

331
00:23:14.753 --> 00:23:15.986
I guess you're right.

332
00:23:15.986 --> 00:23:17.753
What should we buy. then?

333
00:23:18.520 --> 00:23:19.886
Ask your daughter-in-law.

334
00:23:19.886 --> 00:23:23.386
Young moms usually
have a better sense for these things.

335
00:23:23.386 --> 00:23:25.820
What sense? My foot.

336
00:23:25.820 --> 00:23:29.753
She showed up empty-handed
the first time she came to meet

337
00:23:29.753 --> 00:23:31.120
her future mother-in-law.

338
00:23:31.120 --> 00:23:35.053
One time. I asked her to buy
some red ginseng as a gift.

339
00:23:35.053 --> 00:23:38.220
and she brought back
a whole fresh ginseng root instead.

340
00:23:38.220 --> 00:23:41.153
Come on. no way!

341
00:23:44.153 --> 00:23:46.753
My sister-in-law is just a little unusual.

342
00:23:46.753 --> 00:23:49.686
Sometimes she just doesn't know things
everyone else does.

343
00:23:49.686 --> 00:23:51.386
Really?

344
00:23:54.386 --> 00:23:56.220
Well. that's probably
because she's an orphan.

345
00:23:56.220 --> 00:23:59.853
She didn't have parents
to learn those things from.

346
00:23:59.853 --> 00:24:01.753
Bye.

347
00:24:02.720 --> 00:24:05.420
Oh. what do you mean help?

348
00:24:05.420 --> 00:24:08.853
She couldn't even stick around and ran off...

349
00:24:12.753 --> 00:24:16.053
When did she chop all of this?

350
00:24:16.053 --> 00:24:18.320
Look at how even they are.

351
00:24:18.320 --> 00:24:21.586
How can this...

352
00:24:21.586 --> 00:24:23.553
I'm scared.

353
00:24:23.553 --> 00:24:25.553
- What's this?
- What is going on?

354
00:24:25.553 --> 00:24:27.686
[Black Beans]

355
00:24:27.686 --> 00:24:28.786
Black beans...

356
00:24:28.786 --> 00:24:30.753
[Today Only: Unbeatable Price.
50% Off All Agricultural Products]

357
00:24:30.753 --> 00:24:33.486
- These onions are nice and big.
- They're so cheap.

358
00:24:33.486 --> 00:24:35.620
- The autumn squash is a good price.
- Oh. my.

359
00:24:35.620 --> 00:24:38.486
They're doing something over there too.
Let's go check it out.

360
00:24:46.320 --> 00:24:48.053
Miss Kim!

361
00:24:49.453 --> 00:24:51.553
What are you doing after work?

362
00:24:51.553 --> 00:24:53.420
I asked what you're doing afterward.

363
00:24:53.420 --> 00:24:55.053
Why are you acting like this?

364
00:24:55.053 --> 00:24:58.753
Come on. just stay a minute.
You like this. don't you?

365
00:24:58.753 --> 00:25:00.753
Please don't do this.

366
00:25:02.620 --> 00:25:04.486
I'll get going now.

367
00:25:09.853 --> 00:25:11.620
Who was that?

368
00:25:14.053 --> 00:25:15.920
Miss Kim!

369
00:25:22.753 --> 00:25:24.353
Oh. my back!

370
00:25:24.353 --> 00:25:26.086
[Trash Can Deodorizer]
Who did this?

371
00:25:26.086 --> 00:25:27.853
Who was it?

372
00:25:32.053 --> 00:25:33.653
Oh. my.

373
00:25:34.320 --> 00:25:36.420
<i>Now. for the next 30 minutes only.</i>

374
00:25:36.420 --> 00:25:38.553
<i>we're offering our seasonal
health-boosting samgyetang</i>

375
00:25:38.553 --> 00:25:41.953
<i>at a special buy-one-get-one deal.</i>

376
00:25:41.953 --> 00:25:44.153
Got the samgyetang!

377
00:25:54.721 --> 00:25:55.890
[Big Precious]

378
00:25:58.953 --> 00:26:03.186
Honey. I love you!
I'll really make it up to you.

379
00:26:13.886 --> 00:26:17.720
Wow. my wife really saw it coming.

380
00:26:17.720 --> 00:26:20.520
[Musan Soryong Nightclub]

381
00:26:20.520 --> 00:26:23.153
Wait. get out. Get out.

382
00:26:23.153 --> 00:26:24.720
Come here. I need to wipe your feet.

383
00:26:24.720 --> 00:26:26.453
No. I don't want to!

384
00:26:26.453 --> 00:26:28.753
Yul. come here! You have to wipe your feet.

385
00:26:28.753 --> 00:26:30.653
You'll catch a cold. Hurry.

386
00:26:31.953 --> 00:26:34.886
Okay. Then stay right there.

387
00:26:44.953 --> 00:26:48.553
<i>Honey. I'm in Musan right now.</i>

388
00:26:48.553 --> 00:26:51.986
<i>Something urgent came up
for a business trip. so I might be late.</i>

389
00:26:52.820 --> 00:26:56.986
<i>I was supposed to get home early
and help you... I'm sorry.</i>

390
00:26:56.986 --> 00:26:59.286
<i>I'll take the last bus and come.
even if I'm late.</i>

391
00:26:59.286 --> 00:27:01.186
<i>I love you. Bo Na.</i>

392
00:27:01.186 --> 00:27:03.320
<i>You know how much I love you. right?</i>

393
00:27:03.320 --> 00:27:05.786
Oh. this man. seriously...

394
00:27:14.286 --> 00:27:16.986
Just wait until you get home.
You're not getting away with this.

395
00:27:16.986 --> 00:27:20.186
<i>It can't be helped. It's okay.</i>

396
00:27:20.186 --> 00:27:22.086
<i>Take care of your work and don't worry.</i>

397
00:27:22.086 --> 00:27:24.253
<i>Just stop sending those crying emojis.</i>

398
00:27:30.720 --> 00:27:32.520
Yul. let's get dressed now!

399
00:27:32.520 --> 00:27:33.820
- Come here.
- No. I don't want to.

400
00:27:33.820 --> 00:27:34.820
Come here!

401
00:27:34.820 --> 00:27:36.853
- Come on. hurry.
- No!

402
00:27:36.853 --> 00:27:37.953
Come quickly.

403
00:27:37.953 --> 00:27:40.820
Come here! Come here!

404
00:29:05.453 --> 00:29:07.020
Boss. I'll just go use
the bathroom real quick.

405
00:29:07.020 --> 00:29:08.020
You punk!

406
00:29:08.020 --> 00:29:09.786
I'm sorry.

407
00:29:09.786 --> 00:29:11.386
Give it to me!

408
00:29:32.586 --> 00:29:34.886
[Empty Taxi]
Follow that black car. please.

409
00:29:37.120 --> 00:29:38.720
Let's sleep.

410
00:29:38.720 --> 00:29:41.620
I'm going to sleep with Daddy.
When's Daddy coming?

411
00:29:41.620 --> 00:29:44.453
I told you that Daddy is busy with work
and will be late today.

412
00:29:44.453 --> 00:29:46.220
Sleep with me. okay?

413
00:29:46.220 --> 00:29:48.820
No. I'll sleep when Daddy gets home.

414
00:29:48.820 --> 00:29:51.486
Where did Daddy go?

415
00:29:51.486 --> 00:29:54.653
His work isn't finished yet.

416
00:29:54.653 --> 00:29:57.053
Should I sing you a song?

417
00:29:57.053 --> 00:29:58.786
What kind of work?

418
00:30:00.520 --> 00:30:05.153
Daddy is doing...
something very. very important.

419
00:30:05.153 --> 00:30:10.720
He is a truly good man
who does wonderful things for people.

420
00:30:10.720 --> 00:30:12.686
A good person?

421
00:30:12.686 --> 00:30:18.853
Yes. A very good person
who makes the world brighter.

422
00:30:18.853 --> 00:30:19.886
Yeah. honey.

423
00:30:19.886 --> 00:30:21.153
<i>Honey. are you on your way?</i>

424
00:30:21.153 --> 00:30:22.186
Yes. I'm on my way.

425
00:30:22.186 --> 00:30:24.720
<i>I prepared the barbecue.
but I haven't picked out the wine yet.</i>

426
00:30:24.720 --> 00:30:26.520
Barbecue with wine?

427
00:30:26.520 --> 00:30:28.953
Of course. Napa Cabernet.

428
00:30:28.953 --> 00:30:32.786
<i>Napa Cabernet? Okay. I'll get that. then.</i>

429
00:30:32.786 --> 00:30:34.753
<i>How much longer?</i>

430
00:30:43.853 --> 00:30:46.386
How far is he going?

431
00:30:53.653 --> 00:30:55.653
Sir. I'm almost out of time
for the last train.

432
00:30:55.653 --> 00:30:58.553
Is Musan Station far from here?
How long will it take?

433
00:30:58.553 --> 00:31:00.486
What. Musan Station?

434
00:31:15.286 --> 00:31:17.753
Oh. my. what happened here?

435
00:31:20.453 --> 00:31:21.953
Ambulance...

436
00:31:21.953 --> 00:31:24.620
- Call an ambulance. Now!
- Okay.

437
00:31:34.653 --> 00:31:39.286
Yes. hello. There's been
a vehicle explosion here.

438
00:31:46.386 --> 00:31:48.453
Rest in peace.

439
00:31:48.453 --> 00:31:51.686
I can't tell you to be reborn.

440
00:32:13.340 --> 00:32:17.140
Yul. we're late! Yul. get out!

441
00:32:17.748 --> 00:32:20.548
Yul. what did I say today was?

442
00:32:20.548 --> 00:32:22.782
- Your first day back at work!
- Right?

443
00:32:22.782 --> 00:32:26.082
Then who did I say would pick you up
after daycare today?

444
00:32:26.082 --> 00:32:27.148
Ms. Hee Seon!

445
00:32:27.148 --> 00:32:30.215
Yul. our Yul! Why are you so smart?

446
00:32:32.082 --> 00:32:34.015
Let's go. let's go. Hurry.

447
00:32:35.282 --> 00:32:36.915
Hello. Miss!

448
00:32:36.915 --> 00:32:40.148
Oh. my. Yul is a little late today.

449
00:32:40.148 --> 00:32:41.482
You're starting today. right?

450
00:32:41.482 --> 00:32:44.948
Yes. so starting today.
a helper will be picking Yul up.

451
00:32:44.948 --> 00:32:46.848
But it's our first time.
both for me and Yul. so...

452
00:32:46.848 --> 00:32:48.239
Oh. don't worry too much.

453
00:32:48.239 --> 00:32:49.715
I'll keep a close eye on Yul

454
00:32:49.715 --> 00:32:51.348
and contact you right away
if anything happens.

455
00:32:51.348 --> 00:32:52.948
Thank you.

456
00:32:52.948 --> 00:32:54.915
Yul. My Yul.

457
00:32:54.915 --> 00:32:56.382
- Today. too...
- Today. too. with friends...

458
00:32:56.382 --> 00:32:58.082
Get along well!

459
00:32:58.082 --> 00:32:59.548
See you later.

460
00:32:59.548 --> 00:33:00.882
Have a great day. Ma'am. Let's go in.

461
00:33:00.882 --> 00:33:02.782
Mommy. bye-bye!

462
00:33:06.734 --> 00:33:08.399
[Child on Board]

463
00:33:15.115 --> 00:33:17.415
Okay. let's get going.

464
00:33:21.148 --> 00:33:26.048
<i>Last night. a vehicle exploded on
an outer road in Musan while driving.</i>

465
00:33:26.048 --> 00:33:29.515
<i>The driver. a man in his 40s
identified as Mr. Bae. died at the scene.</i>

466
00:33:29.515 --> 00:33:31.982
<i>Police say they have asked the NFS
to analyze the crash vehicle</i>

467
00:33:31.982 --> 00:33:37.782
<i>and perform an autopsy to determine
the details of the brutal case.</i>

468
00:33:37.782 --> 00:33:38.815
<i>In other news.</i>

469
00:33:38.815 --> 00:33:41.748
<i>Hwang. who had been serving time
for allegedly murdering his pregnant wife.</i>

470
00:33:41.748 --> 00:33:44.482
<i>has been released after three years.
sparking controversy.</i>

471
00:33:44.482 --> 00:33:47.648
<i>Three years ago. Hwang caused
an accident while driving drunk</i>

472
00:33:47.648 --> 00:33:52.515
<i>and was arrested for killing
his pregnant wife in the passenger seat.</i>

473
00:34:02.682 --> 00:34:04.415
What time is it now?

474
00:34:10.048 --> 00:34:13.415
<i>Honey. I missed the last train.</i>

475
00:34:13.415 --> 00:34:16.448
<i>I have some additional reporting to do.
so I think I need to stay here one more day.</i>

476
00:34:16.448 --> 00:34:18.848
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

477
00:34:18.848 --> 00:34:21.315
Just wait till you get home. Kwon Tae Seong.

478
00:34:30.115 --> 00:34:31.882
It's pretty.

479
00:34:33.148 --> 00:34:35.471
[Durumi Electronics]

480
00:34:41.148 --> 00:34:43.378
[Yoo Bo Na]

481
00:34:54.215 --> 00:34:56.847
[Durumi Electronics]

482
00:35:08.748 --> 00:35:10.115
Excuse me...

483
00:35:10.115 --> 00:35:12.615
What are you doing? Aren't you going in?

484
00:35:12.615 --> 00:35:16.248
Oh. this is so old.

485
00:35:16.248 --> 00:35:17.882
Excuse...

486
00:35:19.682 --> 00:35:21.551
I opened it temporarily for one day.

487
00:35:21.551 --> 00:35:23.782
You can get your new ID badge later.

488
00:35:23.782 --> 00:35:25.415
Pretty good.

489
00:35:33.415 --> 00:35:35.282
Ki Yeong Do. it's been a while.

490
00:35:35.282 --> 00:35:37.182
I'm Assistant Manager Ki.

491
00:35:37.182 --> 00:35:39.248
- What?
- It's been a while since I got promoted.

492
00:35:39.248 --> 00:35:43.615
You got promoted?
Congratulations. Assistant Manager Ki.

493
00:35:43.615 --> 00:35:44.815
You look great.

494
00:35:44.815 --> 00:35:46.648
You haven't changed a bit either.

495
00:35:46.648 --> 00:35:48.882
Really? I couldn't sleep last night.

496
00:35:48.882 --> 00:35:51.082
Why couldn't you sleep?

497
00:35:52.115 --> 00:35:54.615
- Because I heard you were coming back.
- Here it is.

498
00:35:55.782 --> 00:35:57.382
Let's go!

499
00:36:02.448 --> 00:36:05.148
Welcome back!

500
00:36:08.876 --> 00:36:10.415
[Welcome Back. Director Yoo Bo Na]

501
00:36:10.415 --> 00:36:11.882
You're finally back.

502
00:36:11.882 --> 00:36:15.348
Our Director Yoo Bo Na.
whom I've only heard about.

503
00:36:16.282 --> 00:36:18.048
Thank you.

504
00:36:20.215 --> 00:36:22.115
This is Assistant Manager Yang Ye Sol.
who joined while you were away.

505
00:36:22.115 --> 00:36:24.748
She took over from Jeong In Joo.

506
00:36:24.748 --> 00:36:26.548
I've heard so much about you.

507
00:36:26.548 --> 00:36:28.448
I heard you used to be the best on our team.

508
00:36:28.448 --> 00:36:31.915
I've seriously been waiting forever
to meet you.

509
00:36:31.915 --> 00:36:35.148
Not because of your performance or anything.

510
00:36:35.148 --> 00:36:38.715
Anyway. it's really great
to finally meet you.

511
00:36:38.715 --> 00:36:41.815
It's so good to meet you too.

512
00:36:44.615 --> 00:36:47.048
Manager Go. you've been
doing well too. right?

513
00:36:47.048 --> 00:36:48.782
Oh. yeah.

514
00:36:48.782 --> 00:36:51.315
You're finally back. Director Yoo.

515
00:36:53.182 --> 00:36:55.348
I'll head to my desk.

516
00:37:09.082 --> 00:37:10.582
Is the team leader not here yet?

517
00:37:10.582 --> 00:37:13.182
Oh. he went on a business trip
to Musan yesterday.

518
00:37:13.182 --> 00:37:15.382
He got back early this morning.
so he'll be a little late.

519
00:37:15.382 --> 00:37:17.282
Musan?

520
00:37:17.282 --> 00:37:19.415
Oh. I see.

521
00:37:21.382 --> 00:37:23.582
Is he still the same?

522
00:37:23.582 --> 00:37:25.482
Still the same.

523
00:37:25.482 --> 00:37:26.782
You're here?

524
00:37:26.782 --> 00:37:30.048
- You're here?
- Hi! Good morning!

525
00:37:30.048 --> 00:37:31.782
You swept the market again. huh?

526
00:37:31.782 --> 00:37:33.848
What is it this time. Team Leader?

527
00:37:36.182 --> 00:37:40.182
Lettuce. Look how fresh it is.

528
00:37:40.182 --> 00:37:41.948
Ms. Yoo Bo Na is here.

529
00:37:41.948 --> 00:37:43.582
What?

530
00:37:44.748 --> 00:37:46.548
Director Yoo!

531
00:37:52.115 --> 00:37:55.215
Wow. how long has it been?

532
00:37:55.215 --> 00:37:58.815
You're finally back! Our team's ace.

533
00:37:58.815 --> 00:38:01.582
Have you been well?

534
00:38:01.582 --> 00:38:04.048
You're still the same. Team Leader.

535
00:38:05.815 --> 00:38:11.282
Wow. with Director Yoo back.
the office feels full and lively.

536
00:38:11.282 --> 00:38:15.215
A person needs to have some presence.

537
00:38:16.015 --> 00:38:20.315
Oh. right. We'll catch up properly
when we have the time and money.

538
00:38:20.315 --> 00:38:24.748
But today. I have something
urgent on my mind.

539
00:38:26.348 --> 00:38:28.215
Welcome back.

540
00:38:30.148 --> 00:38:32.548
Alright. get back to work!

541
00:38:35.760 --> 00:38:38.449
[Musan City Police Station]

542
00:38:39.759 --> 00:38:40.914
[A Safe. Clean Sea of Hope]

543
00:38:55.148 --> 00:38:58.015
Excuse me. excuse me!

544
00:38:58.015 --> 00:39:00.682
I heard you were at the scene.
May I have your name?

545
00:39:00.682 --> 00:39:03.382
Oh. yes. Just a moment.

546
00:39:04.915 --> 00:39:08.148
I'm Kwon Tae Seong. a reporter
from Digging Deep News. Not Today.

547
00:39:08.148 --> 00:39:09.615
[Not Today Reporter. Kwon Tae Seong]
What's your name. sir?

548
00:39:09.615 --> 00:39:14.215
Well. what brings an investigative reporter
all the way from Seoul to Musan?

549
00:39:14.215 --> 00:39:16.015
Has the victim's identity been confirmed yet?

550
00:39:16.015 --> 00:39:19.048
What on earth is going on here?

551
00:39:19.048 --> 00:39:20.982
I think that's something
I should be asking you.

552
00:39:20.982 --> 00:39:23.182
So what exactly happened here?

553
00:39:23.182 --> 00:39:24.315
Excuse me?

554
00:39:24.315 --> 00:39:26.382
Well. the taxi driver said

555
00:39:26.382 --> 00:39:29.948
you came out of a club
and suddenly asked him to follow this car.

556
00:39:29.948 --> 00:39:31.582
So. what was that about?

557
00:39:31.582 --> 00:39:34.482
Well. what else would a reporter be doing?
I was covering a story.

558
00:39:34.482 --> 00:39:35.482
Like I am now.

559
00:39:35.482 --> 00:39:38.148
A story? What kind of story?

560
00:39:40.348 --> 00:39:43.948
We received information that a new type
of drug had infiltrated clubs around Musan.

561
00:39:43.948 --> 00:39:46.748
So I was meeting an informant today
for an interview. when...

562
00:39:46.748 --> 00:39:49.448
Oh. then what about the car?

563
00:39:49.448 --> 00:39:51.515
Why did you follow it?

564
00:39:53.715 --> 00:39:56.682
Am I a witness? A person of interest?

565
00:39:57.315 --> 00:39:58.748
Or am I a suspect?

566
00:39:58.748 --> 00:40:01.982
No. it's not like that.
Just tell me what happened...

567
00:40:01.982 --> 00:40:04.182
The informant said that man was a dropper.

568
00:40:04.182 --> 00:40:06.148
- A dropper?
- I was following him

569
00:40:06.148 --> 00:40:10.315
in case I could catch him
distributing drugs to other clubs.

570
00:40:10.315 --> 00:40:12.015
Drug-related reports

571
00:40:12.015 --> 00:40:16.348
tend to focus sensationally
on ordinary users consuming drugs.

572
00:40:16.348 --> 00:40:19.648
But I wanted to focus on the suppliers

573
00:40:19.648 --> 00:40:21.748
and expose how these drugs are distributed.

574
00:40:21.748 --> 00:40:23.748
I thought it could raise public awareness

575
00:40:23.748 --> 00:40:28.482
and also help your investigations
and arrests in making society safer.

576
00:40:28.482 --> 00:40:30.115
Does that answer your question?

577
00:40:31.182 --> 00:40:33.748
Oh. yeah. That's admirable.

578
00:40:33.748 --> 00:40:37.882
But if he's a dropper. isn't he just
a low-level errand boy who delivers drugs?

579
00:40:37.882 --> 00:40:42.048
Oh. dear. Mr. Reporter.
I guess you've got the wrong idea.

580
00:40:42.048 --> 00:40:44.515
- Pardon?
- For now. go home.

581
00:40:44.515 --> 00:40:45.903
We may contact you later
for a witness interview.

582
00:40:45.903 --> 00:40:48.448
so please be aware of that.

583
00:40:48.448 --> 00:40:51.248
As you can see.
the scene is a mess right now. I'm off.

584
00:40:51.248 --> 00:40:55.115
Please make sure you take
thorough photos of the scene.

585
00:40:57.200 --> 00:40:58.344
[Son Seok Gu]

586
00:41:05.248 --> 00:41:06.248
- Hello...
- <i>Why do you keep calling?</i>

587
00:41:06.248 --> 00:41:07.382
You're putting me in a difficult position.

588
00:41:07.382 --> 00:41:10.015
I've called you several times.
Why haven't you answered?

589
00:41:10.015 --> 00:41:13.582
I need to see you right now. Where are you?

590
00:41:13.582 --> 00:41:16.882
Meet? What for? It's chaos here
because of what happened.

591
00:41:16.882 --> 00:41:18.915
Don't contact me again.
I'm changing my number.

592
00:41:18.915 --> 00:41:21.982
Wait. hold on! Let me ask you just one thing.

593
00:41:21.982 --> 00:41:25.215
What happened to that dropper from yesterday?

594
00:41:25.215 --> 00:41:27.915
<i>Why are you asking about him?</i>

595
00:41:27.915 --> 00:41:31.682
He came back shortly
after you left yesterday.

596
00:41:31.682 --> 00:41:33.015
- Well. then...
- <i>I'm hanging up.</i>

597
00:41:33.015 --> 00:41:34.615
Hello...

598
00:41:49.682 --> 00:41:51.682
That persistent guy actually showed up.

599
00:41:51.682 --> 00:41:55.215
I told you over the phone
several times that it's not possible.

600
00:41:55.215 --> 00:41:56.882
Who was the victim in last night's incident?

601
00:41:56.882 --> 00:41:59.782
Jeez. what kind of reporter is so pushy...

602
00:42:03.482 --> 00:42:06.615
I'm the one who witnessed
the scene firsthand. Look at me.

603
00:42:06.615 --> 00:42:08.015
I still feel sick to my stomach.

604
00:42:08.015 --> 00:42:12.348
Well. if you feel sick. you can go to
a pharmacy and get some medicine.

605
00:42:12.348 --> 00:42:13.948
I even betrayed my wife.

606
00:42:13.948 --> 00:42:18.382
I was supposed to get home
no matter what yesterday.

607
00:42:18.382 --> 00:42:20.748
Then hurry home now.

608
00:42:20.748 --> 00:42:22.948
Come on. it's already too late.

609
00:42:22.948 --> 00:42:26.515
Today was my wife's first day back at work.

610
00:42:26.515 --> 00:42:28.582
Sir. are you married? My daughter is four.

611
00:42:28.582 --> 00:42:32.548
Why are you telling me
your daughter is four right now?

612
00:42:32.548 --> 00:42:34.715
I mean. it's not really relevant...

613
00:42:34.715 --> 00:42:37.515
Anyway. the victim. Mr. Bae.
is the drug kingpin Bae Doo Hyuk. right?

614
00:42:37.515 --> 00:42:40.248
Well. that's true. but...

615
00:42:41.982 --> 00:42:44.282
Come on.

616
00:42:44.282 --> 00:42:48.367
Was this just an accident?
Or... was it possibly murder?

617
00:42:51.311 --> 00:42:52.448
Come out.

618
00:42:52.448 --> 00:42:53.715
- Is that right?
- Come out!

619
00:42:53.715 --> 00:42:54.782
Please just tell me once.

620
00:42:54.782 --> 00:42:56.915
I said come out. Come out.

621
00:42:56.915 --> 00:42:59.848
- Well. Director Yoo.
- Yes?

622
00:42:59.848 --> 00:43:02.482
I feel bad asking this
on your first day back.

623
00:43:02.482 --> 00:43:06.882
but today. could you do a client meeting?

624
00:43:08.582 --> 00:43:09.848
Today. right away?

625
00:43:09.848 --> 00:43:11.315
Yeah. today.

626
00:43:11.315 --> 00:43:13.115
I know it's a lot to ask on your first day.

627
00:43:13.115 --> 00:43:16.148
And I know you're not someone
who does things halfway.

628
00:43:16.148 --> 00:43:20.382
But the client said today is
the only time they can make it.

629
00:43:20.382 --> 00:43:23.448
Assistant Manager Ki prepared everything.

630
00:43:25.148 --> 00:43:29.215
You just need to handle the meeting.

631
00:43:29.215 --> 00:43:30.542
[Client Report]

632
00:43:45.048 --> 00:43:46.548
You prepared everything thoroughly.

633
00:43:46.548 --> 00:43:48.648
I learned well from you.

634
00:43:52.048 --> 00:43:53.915
Let's do it during the day.

635
00:43:55.048 --> 00:43:56.382
During the day? Why?

636
00:43:56.382 --> 00:43:59.548
Considering the meeting location
and the client's schedule.

637
00:43:59.548 --> 00:44:01.248
having thought about it in detail.

638
00:44:01.248 --> 00:44:05.348
do you think it's strategically better
to do it during the day. Director Yoo?

639
00:44:05.348 --> 00:44:07.748
I have to pick up my kid.

640
00:44:09.715 --> 00:44:11.915
My husband is going to be late today.

641
00:44:15.515 --> 00:44:18.382
Let's do it during the day.

642
00:44:21.997 --> 00:44:24.687
[Client Information]

643
00:44:30.582 --> 00:44:35.215
Whether it's an accident or murder.
we'll know after the NFS results come out.

644
00:44:35.215 --> 00:44:38.982
And I wasn't the one who told you
the victim's name. okay?

645
00:44:46.825 --> 00:44:48.548
[A Safe. Clean Sea of Hope]

646
00:44:48.548 --> 00:44:51.082
Please take me to
the Musan Forensic Science Institute.

647
00:45:16.782 --> 00:45:19.248
I like the meeting venue.

648
00:45:20.482 --> 00:45:23.215
<i>The client arrived an hour ago
and is waiting inside.</i>

649
00:45:23.215 --> 00:45:24.215
<i>You can go right in.</i>

650
00:45:24.215 --> 00:45:26.582
Okay. let's see what you've got.

651
00:45:26.582 --> 00:45:28.582
Me?

652
00:45:28.582 --> 00:45:29.848
Oh. come on. Of course. I...

653
00:45:29.848 --> 00:45:31.982
Not you. me.

654
00:45:32.982 --> 00:45:35.048
Are you nervous?

655
00:45:35.048 --> 00:45:37.915
<i>Well. I guess it has been a while.</i>

656
00:45:37.915 --> 00:45:39.682
That's true for you.

657
00:45:39.682 --> 00:45:41.682
Stop shaking your leg.

658
00:45:55.382 --> 00:45:58.148
You too. Team Leader. Relax your grip.

659
00:46:19.231 --> 00:46:20.091
[Please Hear Our Prayer]

660
00:46:20.115 --> 00:46:21.948
Have you ever prayed?

661
00:46:21.948 --> 00:46:24.215
Of course not. What about you?

662
00:46:24.215 --> 00:46:28.015
Sometimes. without realizing it.
during moments that really shake me.

663
00:46:30.182 --> 00:46:33.715
You have moments like that too? When?

664
00:46:33.715 --> 00:46:37.982
When the child is chewing on
something and eating.

665
00:46:58.082 --> 00:47:00.215
<i>Isn't it a good thing if the child eats well?</i>

666
00:47:00.215 --> 00:47:02.682
The problem is that I never gave
the child anything to eat.

667
00:47:02.682 --> 00:47:05.248
Nothing has ever scared me
more than that moment.

668
00:47:14.682 --> 00:47:17.882
<i>You should see a long bench
in the right corner.</i>

669
00:47:17.882 --> 00:47:19.515
Yeah. I see it.

670
00:47:21.748 --> 00:47:26.082
Do you know when it's hardest
to comfort a crying four-year-old?

671
00:47:26.082 --> 00:47:29.148
- <i>When?</i>
- When a friend gets hurt at daycare.

672
00:47:29.148 --> 00:47:31.482
Oh. out of sadness?

673
00:47:31.482 --> 00:47:36.348
No. guilt. She thought
it was her fault and cried for an hour.

674
00:47:36.348 --> 00:47:38.815
Come on. what does a four-year-old even know?

675
00:47:38.815 --> 00:47:41.048
They know. Even four-year-olds.

676
00:47:41.048 --> 00:47:42.082
What?

677
00:47:42.082 --> 00:47:46.815
They know that they shouldn't
hurt someone. even by accident.

678
00:47:48.782 --> 00:47:50.715
Okay. shall we go?

679
00:47:53.282 --> 00:47:55.182
Now is a good time.

680
00:48:37.248 --> 00:48:41.748
Sales Team 3. Yoo Bo Na.
starting client meeting.

681
00:49:32.948 --> 00:49:34.815
Meeting concluded.

682
00:49:54.882 --> 00:49:57.048
Still got it.

683
00:50:12.415 --> 00:50:14.548
Rest in peace.

684
00:50:16.115 --> 00:50:19.248
I can't tell you to be reborn.

685
00:50:39.415 --> 00:50:42.082
Yoo Bo Na comes back.

686
00:51:03.917 --> 00:51:07.150
- Yul.
- Mommy!

687
00:51:07.150 --> 00:51:08.750
Yul!

688
00:51:08.750 --> 00:51:10.950
- Chae Won. hello.
- Hello.

689
00:51:10.950 --> 00:51:13.517
Did you have fun playing with Chae Won today?

690
00:51:13.517 --> 00:51:15.983
Yeah. I made this with her.

691
00:51:15.983 --> 00:51:17.017
Mommy. it's a present for you!

692
00:51:17.017 --> 00:51:19.750
What is this? Is it a rose?

693
00:51:19.750 --> 00:51:20.850
Yeah.

694
00:51:20.850 --> 00:51:22.383
But it's not my birthday today.

695
00:51:22.383 --> 00:51:25.650
I told her you had a hard first day
back at work. and she made this.

696
00:51:25.650 --> 00:51:28.283
Oh. you did that. Yul?

697
00:51:28.283 --> 00:51:29.783
You like flowers.

698
00:51:29.783 --> 00:51:31.883
Yes. that's right! You're the best. Yul.

699
00:51:31.883 --> 00:51:34.317
My Yul is the best! Thank you.

700
00:51:34.317 --> 00:51:36.950
Let me see. Yul. It looks just like you.

701
00:51:36.950 --> 00:51:39.783
Oh. you're so cute.

702
00:51:39.783 --> 00:51:41.583
Thank you!

703
00:51:42.217 --> 00:51:44.250
Let's go home now. okay?

704
00:51:55.517 --> 00:51:58.017
What concept is this supposed to be?

705
00:51:58.017 --> 00:52:00.983
It's the kind of face you talk about
when you say someone has no shame.

706
00:52:00.983 --> 00:52:03.850
It's not funny at all. Stop it.

707
00:52:08.883 --> 00:52:10.717
Honey. I'm sorry...

708
00:52:10.717 --> 00:52:14.250
I'll go without soup for a month.
I think I can handle it.

709
00:52:14.250 --> 00:52:15.917
Will that be enough?

710
00:52:15.917 --> 00:52:17.950
Not enough?

711
00:52:17.950 --> 00:52:19.883
I'm really sorry.

712
00:52:20.583 --> 00:52:22.450
What exactly are you sorry for?

713
00:52:23.783 --> 00:52:27.683
I mean. I really was going to come home.
even if it was late. but...

714
00:52:27.683 --> 00:52:29.617
Oh. is that all you have to say?

715
00:52:33.150 --> 00:52:35.083
I was going to come home
no matter how late it was.

716
00:52:35.083 --> 00:52:38.317
I even booked the last train ticket.

717
00:52:38.317 --> 00:52:40.650
How could you do this to me?

718
00:52:40.650 --> 00:52:41.850
That's how reporting is. you know.

719
00:52:41.850 --> 00:52:42.930
Once a story breaks.

720
00:52:42.930 --> 00:52:46.050
one thing leads to another.
and it just keeps snowballing...

721
00:52:46.050 --> 00:52:48.383
How could you only buy something for Yul?

722
00:52:48.383 --> 00:52:49.983
What?

723
00:52:52.850 --> 00:52:58.117
Yul. you can only have two. No more. okay?

724
00:52:59.783 --> 00:53:03.550
How could you only buy
the cream-flavored walnut cakes?

725
00:53:05.217 --> 00:53:07.883
You like red bean filling. right?

726
00:53:07.883 --> 00:53:09.383
I really do.

727
00:53:09.383 --> 00:53:11.950
Ever since we first met
about seven years ago.

728
00:53:11.950 --> 00:53:16.050
I think I've only eaten red bean bread.
red bean porridge. and red bean noodles...

729
00:53:16.050 --> 00:53:18.583
Did you already forget that?

730
00:53:18.583 --> 00:53:20.117
I remember.

731
00:53:20.117 --> 00:53:22.417
But how could you...

732
00:53:22.417 --> 00:53:27.250
Yul. put that down.
No. you can't have more than two.

733
00:53:27.250 --> 00:53:28.450
Eat it after dinner.

734
00:53:28.450 --> 00:53:30.117
Okay.

735
00:53:30.983 --> 00:53:33.850
But how could you...

736
00:53:33.850 --> 00:53:37.183
This is the mouth that has no excuses.

737
00:53:37.950 --> 00:53:39.717
- You laughed!
- No. I didn't.

738
00:53:39.717 --> 00:53:41.183
Huh? You laughed.

739
00:53:41.183 --> 00:53:42.917
You laughed! It's over when you smile.

740
00:53:42.917 --> 00:53:45.183
Yul. Mommy laughed!

741
00:53:47.283 --> 00:53:49.583
I'm letting it slide because of Yul. okay?

742
00:53:49.583 --> 00:53:52.417
I'm letting it go because Yul
helped make things easier for me.

743
00:53:52.417 --> 00:53:54.150
Yeah.

744
00:53:59.883 --> 00:54:03.617
Yul did that? Did you help Mommy
even for Daddy's sake?

745
00:54:03.617 --> 00:54:06.317
Oh. my. so cute!

746
00:54:06.317 --> 00:54:09.217
No. wash your hands before touching her.
Yul already took a bath.

747
00:54:09.217 --> 00:54:11.450
I won't touch her. I'll just hug her.

748
00:54:11.450 --> 00:54:14.017
You're my precious treasure.

749
00:54:14.017 --> 00:54:16.183
Right. how was your first day back at work?

750
00:54:16.183 --> 00:54:17.183
After such a long time...

751
00:54:17.183 --> 00:54:19.117
Yul. let's eat after dinner.

752
00:54:19.117 --> 00:54:21.583
- You'll get scolded by Mommy.
- Well. everyone helped me out.

753
00:54:21.583 --> 00:54:24.483
Still. it's something I've done for
a long time. so it came back quickly.

754
00:54:24.483 --> 00:54:27.150
I knew you'd do great. I told you. right?

755
00:54:27.150 --> 00:54:29.350
You'd get back into
the swing of things quickly.

756
00:54:31.250 --> 00:54:34.717
Honey. go wash up quickly. We need to eat.

757
00:54:34.717 --> 00:54:37.683
No. you're tired.
Let's just make do with this today.

758
00:54:37.683 --> 00:54:40.817
Sure. if you say so.
But it's still samgyetang.

759
00:54:40.817 --> 00:54:42.717
Samgyetang?

760
00:54:43.917 --> 00:54:45.583
Yul. she says it's samgyetang.

761
00:54:45.583 --> 00:54:47.817
I will go wash up quickly. okay?

762
00:54:55.817 --> 00:54:57.717
<i>The tenant from Tae Seong Chicken
on the first floor</i>

763
00:54:57.717 --> 00:55:02.017
<i>wanted to visit and greet you in person.
but I declined on your behalf.</i>

764
00:55:02.017 --> 00:55:06.517
<i>But they want to send you a gift.
What should I do?</i>

765
00:55:12.083 --> 00:55:13.817
Honey. can you get me a towel?

766
00:55:13.817 --> 00:55:15.783
Yeah. hold on!

767
00:55:17.083 --> 00:55:18.850
<i>Please politely decline.</i>

768
00:55:18.850 --> 00:55:21.850
<i>And I'll also freeze the rent for next month.</i>

769
00:55:21.850 --> 00:55:23.883
- Thank you for the meal!
- Eat plenty.

770
00:55:23.883 --> 00:55:25.650
Yul. try this.

771
00:55:26.650 --> 00:55:27.983
- Is it good?
- Yeah.

772
00:55:27.983 --> 00:55:29.394
It's super. super good!

773
00:55:29.394 --> 00:55:31.550
Super. super good?

774
00:55:31.550 --> 00:55:33.817
But Yul. didn't you miss Daddy?

775
00:55:33.817 --> 00:55:35.383
- I missed you!
- How much?

776
00:55:35.383 --> 00:55:36.817
This much!

777
00:55:36.817 --> 00:55:39.050
You missed him this much?

778
00:55:39.050 --> 00:55:41.550
Dance as much as you enjoy the food!

779
00:55:59.090 --> 00:56:03.634
[Ok's Flower Shop]

780
00:56:10.350 --> 00:56:13.383
You're early! Did you change your schedule?

781
00:56:13.383 --> 00:56:15.550
Well. right. You have to go to work now.

782
00:56:15.550 --> 00:56:18.650
Why did you open so early?
The sun isn't even up yet.

783
00:56:18.650 --> 00:56:23.017
I need to catch customers on their way
to work. Making a living is tough.

784
00:56:23.017 --> 00:56:26.817
I thought you'd finally have some free time
after sending your kid to daycare.

785
00:56:26.817 --> 00:56:28.950
How does it feel to be back?

786
00:56:30.117 --> 00:56:31.583
My life is about to get a lot busier.

787
00:56:31.583 --> 00:56:34.650
And the world will get noisier. huh?

788
00:56:37.517 --> 00:56:39.183
What flower is this? Is it cosmos?

789
00:56:39.183 --> 00:56:40.183
It's a marguerite.

790
00:56:40.183 --> 00:56:41.217
Oh. marguerite.

791
00:56:41.217 --> 00:56:44.950
Its flower meanings are
"revealing secrets" and "true love."

792
00:56:44.950 --> 00:56:48.717
Come to think of it. this one flower
contains both "secret" and "truth."

793
00:56:48.717 --> 00:56:51.083
"A truthful person has no secrets."

794
00:56:51.083 --> 00:56:54.183
"True love means revealing your secrets."
Is that what it means?

795
00:56:54.183 --> 00:56:57.050
Well. I don't really like that meaning.

796
00:56:57.050 --> 00:57:00.150
Sometimes you keep secrets
because you love someone too much.

797
00:57:02.950 --> 00:57:05.550
Aren't you worried that

798
00:57:05.550 --> 00:57:08.883
the day might come
when your husband finds out?

799
00:57:14.050 --> 00:57:16.783
Well. the night before I went back to work.

800
00:57:16.783 --> 00:57:19.103
my husband promised he'd come home early.

801
00:57:19.103 --> 00:57:21.583
but then he suddenly had to go out of town.

802
00:57:21.583 --> 00:57:24.650
He said he'd come home
even if it was late. but he never did.

803
00:57:24.650 --> 00:57:25.683
Oh. dear.

804
00:57:25.683 --> 00:57:29.017
I knew it was because of his reporting.
but I was still hurt.

805
00:57:29.017 --> 00:57:32.217
I was busy getting ready.
but I just got upset for no reason.

806
00:57:32.217 --> 00:57:35.314
"Kwon Tae Seong. just you wait
till you get home tonight."

807
00:57:35.314 --> 00:57:39.917
There I was. all fired up by myself.
and then I just ended up laughing.

808
00:57:40.750 --> 00:57:43.583
I found myself so strange and amazing.

809
00:57:43.583 --> 00:57:46.583
And I still can't believe moments like that.

810
00:57:47.750 --> 00:57:49.383
I love them.

811
00:57:51.650 --> 00:57:53.883
So I'm not worried.

812
00:57:54.617 --> 00:57:56.950
Because that day will never come.

813
00:58:09.517 --> 00:58:12.683
<i>He's someone who lives in the light.</i>

814
00:58:12.683 --> 00:58:15.550
<i>Because he's different from me.</i>

815
00:58:15.550 --> 00:58:19.083
<i>Because if he knew how different we are.
we couldn't stay together.</i>

816
00:58:19.083 --> 00:58:21.883
You don't really know much about me. do you?

817
00:58:21.883 --> 00:58:23.950
I don't know much about you. Bo Na.

818
00:58:25.083 --> 00:58:27.217
I know your name. but...

819
00:58:28.317 --> 00:58:30.483
I don't even know if it's your real name.

820
00:58:32.083 --> 00:58:35.250
<i>Where you were born. how you grew up...</i>

821
00:58:47.650 --> 00:58:52.417
<i>What your family is like.
or what you do for a living...</i>

822
00:58:57.717 --> 00:58:59.122
<i>Why you were standing there</i>

823
00:58:59.122 --> 00:59:02.017
- <i>on the day we first met?</i>
- Hold on!

824
00:59:02.017 --> 00:59:04.417
- Come down. now!
- <i>I don't know those things either.</i>

825
00:59:04.417 --> 00:59:06.050
Oh. slowly!

826
00:59:06.050 --> 00:59:10.017
But I do know some aspects of you. Bo Na.

827
00:59:10.017 --> 00:59:12.317
Perhaps love begins...

828
00:59:13.317 --> 00:59:15.417
when you find yourself drawn to

829
00:59:15.417 --> 00:59:18.917
just one side of a person
among all the many sides they have.

830
00:59:21.883 --> 00:59:24.383
I've already fallen in love.

831
00:59:31.250 --> 00:59:34.117
My name is Yoo Bo Na. It's my real name.

832
00:59:36.217 --> 00:59:40.650
Please take care of me.
It's my first time with love.

833
00:59:43.083 --> 00:59:46.683
<i>I'm not worried.
Because that day will never come.</i>

834
00:59:46.683 --> 00:59:51.917
<i>Because the day he sees
my other side will never come.</i>

835
00:59:55.250 --> 00:59:56.250
<i>Breaking news.</i>

836
00:59:56.250 --> 01:00:01.383
<i>A shooting using a sniper rifle
has occurred in the heart of Seoul.</i>

837
01:00:01.383 --> 01:00:05.917
<i>Some speculate that Kingfisher.
the infamous serial gun killer</i>

838
01:00:05.917 --> 01:00:08.417
[Breaking News: Kingfisher Returns?]
<i>who disappeared for the past four years.</i>

839
01:00:08.417 --> 01:00:10.717
[Shooting Homicide in Seoul]
<i>may have returned.</i>

840
01:00:10.717 --> 01:00:14.183
<i>The incident took place at a hotel
in Jeonjak-dong. Seoul.</i>

841
01:00:14.183 --> 01:00:16.183
<i>A man in his thirties.
identified as Mr. Hwang.</i>

842
01:00:16.183 --> 01:00:20.783
<i>was struck and killed by a bullet
fired from outside the building.</i>

843
01:00:20.783 --> 01:00:24.117
<i>For more details. we'll soon connect live to
our reporter on the scene</i>

844
01:00:24.117 --> 01:00:26.483
<i>for the latest on the police investigation...</i>

845
01:01:17.411 --> 01:01:20.261
[A Bona Fide Killer]

846
01:01:20.285 --> 01:01:22.050
A gun murder in South Korea?

847
01:01:22.050 --> 01:01:23.650
I think that punk is back.

848
01:01:23.650 --> 01:01:25.717
From now on. you're going
after Kingfisher. right?

849
01:01:25.717 --> 01:01:27.083
I'll really give it my all this time.

850
01:01:27.083 --> 01:01:28.083
Is it really the Kingfisher?

851
01:01:28.083 --> 01:01:29.682
[Musan Drug Kingpin's Car Explosion]
You're covering the Kingfisher story. right?

852
01:01:29.682 --> 01:01:31.217
Like. you find anything at the shooting site.

853
01:01:31.217 --> 01:01:32.283
Did you come here knowing something?

854
01:01:32.283 --> 01:01:34.683
Hey. you never know.
What if that was the real clue?

855
01:01:34.683 --> 01:01:35.730
[I'd like to provide a tip about Kingfisher]
But sometimes.

856
01:01:35.730 --> 01:01:38.017
[Security Alert]
I think that day might actually come.

857
01:01:38.017 --> 01:01:40.017
He might find me.

858
01:01:40.017 --> 01:01:41.183
Shall I schedule a meeting?

859
01:01:41.183 --> 01:01:42.383
Don't you think something's strange?

860
01:01:42.383 --> 01:01:43.922
[Yoo Bo Na. Husband. Company]
Honestly. a guy like him

861
01:01:43.922 --> 01:01:45.682
getting gunned down
by the Kingfisher is just unsurprising.

862
01:01:45.682 --> 01:01:49.883
What would you do if you lost
the things that matter most to you?

863
01:01:52.450 --> 01:01:54.483
Where's Kwon Tae Seong?

864
01:01:55.305 --> 01:02:55.302
